rust-code-style-note-tabs = Reformat Code formats Rust with rustfmt, which indents by its own options below, not by the editor's.
rust-code-style-note-spaces = rustfmt has no stable options for spaces.
rust-code-style-note-wrapping = The options of stable rustfmt; with the Project scheme they are read from and written to the project's rustfmt.toml, with Default (IDE) passed to rustfmt as --config.
rust-code-style-note-blank-lines = The blank line options of rustfmt (blank_lines_upper_bound, blank_lines_lower_bound) are unstable: only nightly rustfmt reads them, from rustfmt.toml.
rust-code-style-note-imports = Optimize Imports runs rust-analyzer's Organize Imports; rustfmt sorts the imports and mod declarations when these are on. Grouping imports (group_imports, imports_granularity) is unstable in rustfmt.
rust-code-style-note-arrangement = Rearrange Code does not reorder Rust code: there are no arrangement rules for Rust yet.
rust-toolchain-error-agent = An agent may not choose the Rust toolchain or rust-analyzer, or a rust-analyzer setting that names a program: it chooses the program that runs. The person can do it in Settings → Languages & Frameworks → Rust.
